     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Provide the MoD with a developed and tested IT system of the State e-Register for Defence Resources. 

2. Support the MoD with gender equality expertise and training for the implementation of the National Action Plan on the implementation of the UN Security Council Resolution 1325 on Women, Peace and Security for 2018-2021.

3. Conduct the procurement of the up-to-date equipment and rehabilitation of physical infrastructure, leading to the MoD&#x2019;s enhanced capacities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The MoD possess State e-Register for Defence Resources able to collect, store, preserve, update and process the data on mobilization resources for its operational needs and in case of emergencies.

2. The MoD is supported in the carrying out the activities of the National Action Plan on the implementation of the UN Security Council Resolution 1325 on Women, Peace and Security for 2018-2021, aimed at mainstreaming the gender equality in the policies and daily activity.

3. The MoD is provided with the planned for procurement in 2020 of the modern equipment and rehabilitated physical infrastructure.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Provide the MoD with a developed and tested IT system of the State e-Register for Defence Resources. 

2. Support the Ministry of Defence with gender equality expertise and trainings for the implementation of the National Action Plan for 2018-2021 on UN Security Council Resolution 1325 Women, Peace and Security .

3. Conduct the procurement of the up-to-date equipment and rehabilitation of physical infrastructure, leading to the MoD&#x2019;s enhanced operational capacities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The State e-Register for Defence Resources (Personnel Module) is commissioned to MoD and is able to collect, store, preserve, update and process the data on mobilization resources for its operational needs and in case of emergencies.

2. The MoD is provided with the requested support for the implementation of the activities of the National Action Plan for 2018-2021 on UN Security Council Resolution 1325 Women, Peace and Security , aimed at mainstreaming the gender equality in the policies and daily activity.

3. Endowment of the MoD with new equipment and modernized physical infrastructure in accordance with its requests for 2021.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Commissioning of the developed and tested IT system of the State e-Register for Defence Resources and its handover to MoD in accordance with the plans for Phase I of development. 

2. Support the Ministry of Defence with the implementation of the National Action Plan on the UN Security Council Resolution 1325 Women, Peace and Security and with enhancing its institutional capacities in addressing gender equality, gender based discrimination and gender based violence.

3. Provide the MoD with up-to-date equipment and modernized physical infrastructure that would enhance its operational capacities and would allow render better services to militaries and civilians.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
